# Question and comparison design

This sensitivity asks whether the exposure patterns and subsequent analyses depend on using questionnaire-derived midsleep on free days corrected for sleep debt (MSFsc). We replace it with **diary-derived corrected midsleep (MSF~sc(diary)~)**, a single timing measure per participant calculated from recorded sleep episodes. Daily phase is still defined relative to that participant's stable timing measure, not the midpoint of each individual night's sleep.

Three analyses separate changes in the timing measure from changes in the available sample:

1. The original questionnaire-MSFsc analysis includes 140 near-eye participants.
2. A matched questionnaire-MSFsc analysis retains only participants with a valid diary night before at least one work day and one free day. Quartiles and all models are refitted on this sample.
3. The MSF~sc(diary)~ analysis uses exactly the same exposure observations as the matched analysis, but recomputes quartiles and relative phase from MSF~sc(diary)~.

A further comparison holds the matched questionnaire quartiles fixed while changing phase alignment to MSF~sc(diary)~. This intermediate scenario separates the timing change from the subsequent reclassification on the same records. It repeats the near-eye phase and daylength models, their inference and diagnostics; the full downstream analyses listed below belong to the two complete matched analyses.

The established questionnaire-based MSFsc measure defines the primary analysis; MSF~sc(diary)~ is a diary-derived correlate used for sensitivity assessment. The Gaussian response, cyclic smooths, random effects, photoperiod terms, autoregressive resets, covariance methods, seeds, and local-support requirement are retained. Clock-time models are also refitted because replacing the timing measure changes chronotype-group membership. Chest measurements, questionnaire-based chronotype sensitivity, predictive validation, attribution, and model-structure sensitivities are repeated in separate output directories.

The [preparation script](sensitivity/diary-msfsc/prepare.R), [scenario driver](sensitivity/diary-msfsc/scenario.R), [generalized interval calculations](sensitivity/diary-msfsc/adapters.R), and [comparison script](sensitivity/diary-msfsc/compare.R) produce the results below. The model fits and covariance simulations are precomputed; this render reads their recorded outputs. The actual producing code is shown beside each analytical stage. A frozen copy of the original R producers is retained in `sensitivity/diary-msfsc/source-snapshot/`.

# Deriving MSF~sc(diary)~

For each diary night, midsleep is the midpoint between sleep onset and final awakening in local wall-clock time. The label comes from the **waking day**: sleep from Saturday to a free Sunday is free-day sleep; sleep from Sunday to a work Monday is work-day sleep. The same upstream interval eligibility and quarantine rules as the diary side-analysis apply. Means use a fixed noon boundary so that nearby sleep times on either side of midnight remain adjacent.

Let $n_W$ and $n_F$ be the numbers of recorded work- and free-day nights, $SD_W$ and $SD_F$ their mean sleep-period durations, and $MS_F$ mean free-day midsleep. We calculate

$$
SD_{all}=\frac{n_W SD_W+n_F SD_F}{n_W+n_F},\qquad
\mathrm{MSF}_{\mathrm{sc(diary)}}=MS_F-\frac{\max(0,SD_F-SD_{all})}{2}.
$$

The work- and free-day means and the observed category counts determine the correction. This is a diary equivalent of MSFsc rather than a complete repeat of MCTQ scoring: the diary input does not identify whether an alarm ended free-day sleep. Participants with only one day type cannot supply the corrected measure and are excluded from both matched analyses.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
paths <- input_paths()
chronotype <- readRDS(paths[["chronotype"]]) |>
  transmute(site, Id, questionnaire_msfsc_hours = as.numeric(msf_sc) / 3600)
diary <- readRDS(paths[["sleepdiaries"]]) |>
  left_join(chronotype, by = c("site", "Id"), relationship = "many-to-one") |>
  mutate(
    participant_key = paste(site, Id, sep = "::"),
    waking_date = as.Date(wake_wall, tz = "UTC"),
    daytype = factor(
      as.character(daytype2),
      levels = c("a work day", "a free day"),
      labels = c("Work", "Free")
    ),
    duration_hours = as.numeric(difftime(
      wake_wall,
      sleep_onset_wall,
      units = "hours"
    )),
    midpoint_wall = sleep_onset_wall + duration_hours * 3600 / 2,
    midsleep_hours = (as.numeric(midpoint_wall) / 3600) %% 24,
    midsleep_unwrapped = ((midsleep_hours + 12) %% 24) - 12,
    eligible_night = is.finite(questionnaire_msfsc_hours) &
      !is.na(sleep_onset_wall) &
      !is.na(wake_wall) &
      sleep_interval_analysis_eligible &
      !sleep_interval_quarantined &
      duration_hours > 0 &
      duration_hours < 24 &
      !is.na(daytype)
  )
valid <- diary |> filter(eligible_night)
stopifnot(!anyDuplicated(valid[c("participant_key", "waking_date")]))
derived <- valid |>
  summarise(
    nights = n(),
    midsleep = mean(midsleep_unwrapped),
    sleep_duration = mean(duration_hours),
    .by = c(site, Id, participant_key, daytype)
  ) |>
  pivot_wider(
    names_from = daytype,
    values_from = c(nights, midsleep, sleep_duration)
  ) |>
  mutate(
    eligible = !is.na(nights_Work) &
      !is.na(nights_Free) &
      nights_Work >= 1L &
      nights_Free >= 1L,
    weighted_sleep_duration = (nights_Work *
      sleep_duration_Work +
      nights_Free * sleep_duration_Free) /
      (nights_Work + nights_Free),
    correction_hours = pmax(0, sleep_duration_Free - weighted_sleep_duration) /
      2,
    diary_msfsc_hours = midsleep_Free - correction_hours
  ) |>
  left_join(chronotype, by = c("site", "Id"), relationship = "one-to-one") |>
  mutate(
    offset_minutes = wrap12(diary_msfsc_hours - questionnaire_msfsc_hours) * 60
  )
write.csv(
  diary,
  file.path(sensitivity_root, "diary-night-registry.csv"),
  row.names = FALSE
)
write.csv(
  derived,
  file.path(sensitivity_root, "derived-msfsc-participants.csv"),
  row.names = FALSE
)
parent_derivation <- read.csv(
  "results/tables/sleep_diary_msfsc_participants.csv"
) |>
  filter(eligible) |>
  select(site, Id, diary_msfsc_hours)
replication <- inner_join(
  filter(derived, eligible),
  parent_derivation,
  by = c("site", "Id"),
  suffix = c("", "_reported"),
  relationship = "one-to-one"
)
stopifnot(
  nrow(replication) == nrow(parent_derivation),
  max(abs(
    replication$diary_msfsc_hours - replication$diary_msfsc_hours_reported
  )) <
    1e-10
)
```
:::



