:::


# Exposure models and contrasts

Both time coordinates use the original full model structure. Near-eye quartile cutoffs also define groups in the chest analysis. Main contrasts have 95% simultaneous coverage across the registered contrast family and all grid points **within each time coordinate**. The four-participant local-support rule is applied separately to every contributing quartile/day-type cell. The primary exposure-curve bands use the original simultaneous-curve convention.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
if (stage == "primary") {
  for (label in c("primary", "chest")) {
    raw <- prepared$frames[[if (label == "primary") "glasses" else "chest"]]
    prep <- fit_preprocess(raw, prepared$cutoffs)
    for (axis in c("clock", "phase")) {
      bundle <- fit_pair(raw, prep, axis, label)
      inference <- infer_curves(bundle)
      inference$individual_draws <- NULL
      atomic_rds(
        inference,
        paste0("results/data/", label, "_", axis, "_inference.rds")
      )
      intervals <- interval_average_contrasts(inference, bundle)
      save_table(intervals, paste0(label, "_", axis, "_interval_averages"))
      diagnose_model(bundle)
      save_table(model_summary(bundle), paste0(label, "_", axis, "_model_fit"))
      rm(bundle, inference)
      gc()
    }
  }
}
```
