```{.r .cell-code}
fixed_primary <- intervals |> filter(window_source == "Original primary fixed", context == "Overall")
fixed_post <- fixed_primary |> filter(phase_label == "Post-MSFsc")
fixed_pre <- fixed_primary |> filter(phase_label == "Pre-MSFsc")
```
:::


On the original fixed windows, the evening-type/morning-type ratio changes from 0.18 to 0.13 pre-MSFsc and from 14.7 to 28.3 post-MSFsc. The direction of both exposure differences is preserved, with larger separation under diary-based classification. These ratios describe the fitted log-scale exposure contrast; their change is not itself a formal between-model test.


::: {#tbl-dmsfsc-work-free .cell tbl-cap='Work/free-day comparisons over the same original primary windows.'}

