# Separating phase alignment from quartile classification {#sec-fixed-groups}

We add an intermediate scenario with **diary-based phase alignment and fixed questionnaire quartiles**. Comparing it with the matched questionnaire analysis changes only alignment; comparing it with the full MSF~sc(diary)~ analysis then changes classification while retaining diary alignment. All three use the same light records, site photoperiod centers, model formulas, standardization weights and support rule. Smoothing parameters and residual autocorrelation are re-estimated for each fit.

Here questionnaire membership means the matched 135-person reference. Its refitted questionnaire cutoffs place three retained participants in a different quartile from the original 140-person analysis. The intermediate scenario preserves every matched-reference assignment.

The [preparation](sensitivity/diary-msfsc/prepare-fixed-groups.R) and [model driver](sensitivity/diary-msfsc/fixed-groups.R) use the frozen model producers. The following code was executed before rendering. It copies questionnaire membership into the diary-timed data and preserves that membership when the shared preprocessing would otherwise assign quartiles again.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
group_columns <- c("quartile", "direction", "extremity", "group_label")
raw <- diary$frames$glasses
reference <- matched$frames$glasses
changing_columns <- c("msf_hours", "phase", "phase_display", group_columns)
unchanged_columns <- setdiff(names(reference), changing_columns)
stopifnot(
  identical(raw[unchanged_columns], reference[unchanged_columns]),
  !anyDuplicated(raw[c("participant_day_key", "clock_bin")])
)
raw[group_columns] <- reference[group_columns]
stopifnot(
  identical(raw[group_columns], reference[group_columns]),
  identical(raw$phase, diary$frames$glasses$phase),
  all(abs(raw$phase - wrap24(raw$clock - raw$diary_msfsc_hours)) < 1e-12),
  all(abs(raw$msf_hours - raw$diary_msfsc_hours) < 1e-12)
)
prepared <- list(
  frames = list(glasses = raw),
  cutoffs = matched$cutoffs,
  participants = distinct(
    raw,
    participant_key,
    quartile,
    direction,
    extremity,
    questionnaire_msfsc_hours,
    diary_msfsc_hours
  ),
  scenario = "dmsfsc-fixed-groups",
  grouping_metric = "Questionnaire MSFsc on the matched sample",
  phase_metric = "Diary-derived dMSFsc",
  signature = digest::digest(list(raw, matched$cutoffs, "fixed-groups-1.0"))
)
```
:::



::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
# The shared preprocessing normally reassigns groups from msf_hours. Use the
# questionnaire value only for classification, then restore diary timing.
original_apply_quartiles <- apply_quartiles
apply_quartiles <- function(x, cutoffs) {
  stopifnot(all(is.finite(x$questionnaire_msfsc_hours)))
  diary_timing <- x$msf_hours
  x$msf_hours <- x$questionnaire_msfsc_hours
  x <- original_apply_quartiles(x, cutoffs)
  x$msf_hours <- diary_timing
  x
}
raw <- prepared$frames$glasses
prep <- fit_preprocess(raw, prepared$cutoffs)
model_data <- apply_preprocess(raw, prep, "phase")
reference <- readRDS("../matched-msfsc/results/models/primary_phase.rds")$data
diary_data <- readRDS("../dmsfsc/results/models/primary_phase.rds")$data
fixed_columns <- setdiff(
  names(reference),
  c("msf_hours", "phase", "phase_display", "t")
)
stopifnot(
  identical(model_data[fixed_columns], reference[fixed_columns]),
  identical(
    model_data[c("t", "phase", "phase_display", "msf_hours")],
    diary_data[c("t", "phase", "phase_display", "msf_hours")]
  )
)
```
