# PRC weighting and the Emens-style balance

The same reconstructed one-hour light PRC is integrated against the estimated extreme-group curves. Published raw and drift-corrected baselines, zero-exposure centering, the original covariance calculation, all five PRC alignment offsets, and the Emens-style regional exposure balance are retained. These are conceptual summaries of exposure timing, not predicted shifts in hours.

The published DLMO-to-MSFsc offsets were established relative to questionnaire MSFsc. Reusing them relative to **MSF~sc(diary)~ is a sensitivity assumption**, not a new calibration of diary midsleep against DLMO. The central offset remains −6.45 h, the published-reference-interval endpoints −6.95 and −5.95 h, and the wider PRC stress tests −8.45 and −4.45 h. The Emens-style calculation retains its three original reference alignments.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
if (stage == "prc") {
  prc <- phase_response_read_prc()
  bundle <- readRDS("results/models/primary_phase.rds")
  inference <- readRDS("results/data/primary_phase_inference.rds")
  result <- phase_response_integrate(prc, bundle, inference)
  phase_response_export(result)
  emens_balance_export(emens_balance(bundle, inference))
}

capture.output(
  sessionInfo(),
  file = paste0("results/provenance/", stage, "_session.txt")
)
save_table(
  tibble(
    stage = stage,
    scenario = scenario,
    started = as.character(started),
    finished = as.character(Sys.time()),
    elapsed_seconds = as.numeric(difftime(Sys.time(), started, units = "secs")),
    prepared_signature = prepared$signature,
    seed = cfg$seed,
    covariance_draws = cfg$draws,
    bootstrap_draws = cfg$bootstrap,
    support_n = cfg$support_n,
    within_coordinate_coverage = cfg$curve_coverage
  ),
  paste0(stage, "_run"),
  "results/provenance"
)
log_step("Completed", scenario, stage)
