# Prediction, attribution and other sensitivities

The five participant-held-out folds and the known-participant final-day holdout are regenerated on the common sample. The two restricted analyses use identical held-out participants and light records. Each training fold estimates its own quartile cutoffs, site photoperiod centers, smoothing parameters and AR correlation. MSF~sc(diary)~ itself is the participant's stable summary of all available diary nights, so validation evaluates held-out **light** prediction conditional on having that diary summary; it does not represent prediction before diary collection.


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
if (stage == "validation") run_validation(prepared)
```
:::



::: {#tbl-dmsfsc-validation .cell tbl-cap='Held-out prediction on the original and restricted samples.'}

```{.r .cell-code}
validation <- comparison("validation_scores")
show_table(validation |> select(scenario, target, axis, RMSE, predictive_R2), digits = 3)
```

