To reproduce, run `Rscript --vanilla sensitivity/diary-msfsc/prepare.R` from the project root. In each scenario directory, run `Rscript --vanilla -e 'source("../scenario.R")'` with the stages `primary`, `validation`, `daylight`, `daylight-validation`, `prc`, `meq`, `sensitivity`, `noncyclic`, `outputs`, and `attribution`, then run `Rscript --vanilla ../verify-stages.R`. Set `MELIDOS_MAIN` and `MELIDOS_R_LIBRARY` to the existing project library paths, as shown in [the run instructions](sensitivity/diary-msfsc/README.md). Finally run `Rscript --vanilla sensitivity/diary-msfsc/compare.R` and render this document. The matched questionnaire primary stage must finish before the MSF~sc(diary)~ daylight stage, which also summarizes its fixed windows.

Each scenario keeps saved fits, prediction draws, contrasts, registries, diagnostics, validations, tables and figures under its own `results/`. Comparison figure data are exported under `sensitivity/diary-msfsc/data/intermediate/`. The [complete interval comparison](sensitivity/diary-msfsc/comparison/phase_interval_averages.csv) retains window selection and local support; [PRC contrasts](sensitivity/diary-msfsc/comparison/prc_contrasts.csv) retain the main group comparisons. [Original-input preservation](sensitivity/diary-msfsc/comparison/original_input_preservation.csv) records the before/after checksums.

For the focused fixed-group extension, run `Rscript --vanilla sensitivity/diary-msfsc/prepare-fixed-groups.R`, then run `Rscript --vanilla -e 'source("../fixed-groups.R")' primary` and the corresponding `daylight` stage inside `dmsfsc-fixed-groups/`. From the project root, `Rscript --vanilla sensitivity/diary-msfsc/compare-fixed-groups.R` produces the fixed-group comparisons. The [run instructions](sensitivity/diary-msfsc/README.md#alignment-with-questionnaire-groups-retained) give the directory and library setup. The new fits, diagnostics, input hashes and R session records stay in that isolated scenario directory.
